# LaTeX build artifacts. The .tex and .pdf are deliverables; these are not, and
# they change on every compile.
*.aux
*.toc
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz

# Sync-client conflict copies. A file-sync client writes `name 2.py` beside
# `name.py`, byte-identical, and 2,520 of them accumulated here -- one of them
# shadowing a script in the faithfulness layer, where a stale copy of a check is
# worse than no copy.
#
# Listed by extension rather than as `* [0-9].*`. That broader pattern also
# swallowed `docs/Chapter 2.pdf` and `data/run 3.json` -- ordinary names that
# happen to end in a space and a digit -- and an ignore rule that hides real
# files is a worse problem than the one it solves.
* [2-9].py
* [2-9].sh
* [2-9].md
* [2-9].json
* [2-9].jsonl
* [2-9].csv
* [2-9].tex
* [2-9].lean
* [2-9].yaml
* [2-9].toml

# This repository ships the corpus. The source repository ignored `*.jsonl` and
# `data/benchmarks/`, which meant a clone did not contain the release the guide
# tells a reader to open -- five of the eight files it named were absent.
!data/release/*.jsonl
!data/benchmarks/**
